## 4. Civil Time

UTC remains canonical internally.

Civil-time conversion is a consumer policy/presentation function.

Production personalization is selected at compile time. A physical UI button
is not part of Dad's build. The `ce_config.hpp` production profile currently
defaults to UTC; no personalized production timezone has been selected. The
existing civil conversion supports Eastern, Central, Mountain, Pacific, and UTC.

Initial supported zones may reuse the existing AAC US timezone logic:

- Eastern
- Central
- Mountain
- Pacific

DST shall be derived from the configured civil timezone and date.

Do not persist "EST" or "EDT" as a setting.

If a timezone is selected in a build, represent the region and derive the active
abbreviation (for example EST/EDT) at runtime.

The active abbreviation should be available to the presentation layer.

