### Serial-only GPS integration diagnostics

The consumer display remains limited to the status language above. Satellite
counts and receiver/debug text are serial diagnostics only and must not be
added to the clock face. Hardware integration should make useful fields
available through a bounded status command, optional verbose diagnostics, or
similarly console-friendly output rather than requiring them all to stream
continuously. Useful fields include:

- receiver state such as NO DATA, ACQUIRING, LOCKED, or STALE;
- satellites used in the fix and, if available, satellites in view;
- fix validity/quality, latest GPS UTC/date, and optional position/altitude in
  verbose bring-up output;
- PPS presence, age, and measured cadence/interval;
- latest valid RMC age, RMC/PPS association state, and useful RMC start or
  completion timing relative to PPS;
- timing-engine state such as QUALIFYING, DISCIPLINED, HOLDOVER, REACQUIRING,
  or HOLDOVER-WARN, plus holdover duration; and
- UART/NMEA activity such as last-byte age, valid sentence count, checksum
  failures, and stale or discarded sentences.

